  "notes": "<p>The We Are the Champions Jam was performed Immediately following the San Francisco Giants winning game seven of the World Series.&nbsp;Yarmouth also&nbsp;included a We Are the Champions tease from Trey. &nbsp;Following a &quot;let&#39;s go Giants&quot; chant after The Wedge, Page congratulated the Giants, adding that he watched the whole series. Trey told the crowd that Page was a Mets fan and that Page watches every Mets game streamed on his phone with many of them on the organ while the band&#39;s playing. Page said&nbsp;&quot;we can&#39;t be world champions all the time&quot; with&nbsp;Fish adding &quot;or ever.&quot; Trey then introduced The Line in honor of the losers in sports.&nbsp;Disease was unfinished. Trey quoted All About That Bass in Contact.</p>",
